  "analysis": [
    "R2955 Draft admits Relation Declaration as a Requirement Form and says it uses the Declaration contract; R2951 Draft declares IS_INVERSE_ALIAS_FOR and is a separate necessary source prerequisite.",
    "Current R2720 limits alias to a declared Relation object and one alias per Relation; its narrow preview extends receiver to inverse model names and one short token per written name. R2817 Draft already has the corresponding successor rule.",
    "Current R2278 qualifies only exact Declaration Form; preview includes admitted specialized Declaration Forms without inventing a Role or string heuristic.",
    "R2469 counts HAS_ACTIVE_SUBJECT while R2278/R2732 use qualified GOVERNS; their relationship is a separate user decision and is not resolved here.",
    "R2732 uses the existing in-list qualifier for exactly Declaration and Relation Declaration; its GOVERNS qualification and endpoint transformation remain unchanged. R2469 is Node-only and needs no change for this Relation Form.",
    "R2247 Current preview makes a narrow inverse-alias model-address exception while preserving qualified derived counterparts as distinct; R2243 Current preview only updates allowed-bound spelling, retaining its existing present-Property value requirement."
  ],
  "integration": [
    "Coordinate Current R2720 with successor R2817 and eventual descriptor retirement; Current R2278 legacy Entity active focus remains another tracked scope hold.",
    "Preserve inverse alias as model address only; no distinct inverse Declaration or automatic endpoint permission."
  ],
  "limits": "No native source, Draft, code, tests, Workflow, Workbench or Git mutation."
}
